{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenID Connect surface controls (X7 G8, plan §4.6\/§4.8; T21.4). Settings that are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"password rules, here because this is the org-baseline-plus-tenant-override surface every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other per-tenant control lives on. They are not all of the same kind as each other, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is which is the whole of what ["},{"code":"validate_tenant_override","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"code":"clamp_overrides_to_org","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] read, so it is set out rather than inferred. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ordered","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant may be stricter than its organization and never more permissive: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"], validated "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disable-only"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — the mirror image of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"mfa_enforced","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", because releasing personal data is the less-restrictive direction, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant can turn its organization’s decision off but never on. * ["},{"code":"Self::saml_idp_enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validated "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disable-only"}]},{"type":"text","text":" exactly like ["},{"code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] (D-20): a tenant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"may turn its organization’s "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" off and never its "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on. * ["},{"code":"Self::ssf_enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validated "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disable-only"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the same way (D-45). * ["},{"code":"Self::dynamic_registration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"], on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ladder "},{"code":"disabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"code":"initial_access_token","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"code":"anonymous","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": a tenant may move down it and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never up. * ["},{"code":"Self::dcr_max_clients","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"code":"Self::dcr_unused_client_ttl_days","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"], on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ordinary "},{"code":"tenant <= org","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rule — with the wrinkle that "},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on the second means "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"never sweep","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is the longest window of all and is handled by ["},{"code":"dcr_ttl_strictness","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ordered"}]},{"type":"text","text":", therefore never validated against the baseline and never clamped: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"code":"Self::default_locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]. A language is a presentation preference; there is no sense in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which Italian is stricter than French. * ["},{"code":"Self::dcr_allowed_scopes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"code":"Self::dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"code":"Self::external_client_allowed_resources","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names per-tenant resources — "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" tenant’s MCP servers, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" tenant’s callback hosts —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and there is no sense in which one such list is stricter than another. A subset rule would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"force an organization to enumerate every tenant’s resource servers in its own baseline"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before any tenant could name one. The model’s rule is “a tenant may only be more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restrictive”, which binds every field that "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"has","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a restrictiveness; a field that has none"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cannot violate it. One cross-field interlock spans both groups and is checked on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resolved policy rather than on either input: see ["},{"code":"validate_dcr_policy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/init(cimd:dcrAllowedRedirectHosts:dcrAllowedScopes:dcrMaxClients:dcrUnusedClientTTLDays:defaultLocale:dynamicRegistration:externalClientAllowedResources:samlIdpEn