xt":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dcrUnusedClientTTLDays":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"T21.4 — how long an externally registered client survives without being used. See","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DEFAULT_DCR_UNUSED_CLIENT_TTL_DAYS"},{"text":"]. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" disables the sweep for this tenant, which an"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"operator who prunes out of band may legitimately want. "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two sweeps read it, over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"different clocks"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (T21.8). A ","type":"text"},{"code":"managed_by: dcr","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" row is measured from its last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"authorization, falling back to when it was registered. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"managed_by: cimd","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" row is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measured from the last time its document was ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"presented","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", which every authorize, token","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and PAR request moves — so a document in daily use is never swept however old its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"registration is, and one nobody has presented since the window is, and re-materialises","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on the next request if it is still published. Like the ceiling, it keeps its ","type":"text"},{"code":"dcr_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"name.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dcrUnusedClientTTLDays"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typ