OidcPolicy"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy","abstract":[{"text":"OpenID Connect surface controls (X7 G8, plan §4.6\/§4.8; T21.4). Settings that are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"password rules, here because this is the org-baseline-plus-tenant-override surface every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other per-tenant control lives on. They are not all of the same kind as each other, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is which is the whole of what [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate_tenant_override"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clamp_overrides_to_org"},{"text":"] read, so it is set out rather than inferred. ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ordered","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant may be stricter than its organization and never more permissive: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"text":"], validated ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"disable-only","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — the mirror image of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mfa_enforced"},{"text":", because releasing personal data is the less-restrictive direction, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant can turn its organization’s decision off but never on. * [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::saml_idp_enabled"},{"text":"],","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"validated ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"disable-only","type":"text"}]},{"text":" exactly like [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"text":"] (D-20): a tenant","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"may turn its organization’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" off and never its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":" on. * [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::ssf_enabled"},{"text":"],","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"validated ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"disable-only","type":"text"}]},{"text":" the same way (D-45). * [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dynamic_registration"},{"text":"], on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ladder ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"disabled"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"initial_access_token"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymous"},{"text":": a tenant may move down it and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never up. * [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_max_clients"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_unused_client_ttl_days"},{"text":"], on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ordinary ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tenant <= org"},{"text":" rule — with the wrinkle that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"text":" on the second means ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never sweep"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is the longest window of all and is handled by [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_ttl_strictness"},{"text":"]. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ordered","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", therefore never validated against the baseline and never clamped: *","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::default_locale"},{"text":"]. A language is a presentation preference; there is no sense in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which Italian is stricter than French. * [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_allowed_scopes"},{"text":"],","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::external_client_allowed_resources"},{"text":"]. Each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names per-tenant resources — ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" tenant’s MCP servers, ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" tenant’s callback hosts —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and there is no sense in which one such list is stricter than another. A subset rule would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"force an organization to enumerate every tenant’s resource servers in its own baseline","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before any tenant could name one. The model’s rule is “a tenant may only be more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"restrictive”, which binds every field that ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"has"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" a restrictiveness; a field that has none","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cannot violate it. One cross-field interlock spans both groups and is checked on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resolved policy rather than on either input: see [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate_dcr_policy"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}],"title":"OidcPolicy","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/sensitiveScopesEnabled":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sensitiveScopesEnabled","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/sensitiveScopesEnabled","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/sensitivescopesenabled","title":"sensitiveScopesEnabled","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether "},{"code":"address","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"phone","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" may be registered on a client, requested at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authorization endpoint, and released at UserInfo (X7 G8). "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Off unless an organization"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"turns it on."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The two scopes release a postal address and a telephone number —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"categories of personal data AXIAM has no other use for — so the deployment that has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never thought about them releases nothing, and the operator who has thought about them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"says so once, at the organization level, where the lawful basis for holding the data was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"decided. The switch is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"capability","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", not a grant: with it on, a client still has to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"register the scope, the request still has to ask for it, and the user still has to have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consented. It is the first of four gates, and it is the only one an operator can close"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for everybody at once."}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/cimd":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cimd"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"CimdPolicy","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK10CimdPolicyV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/cimd","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"T21.5 — whether a URL-shaped "},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is resolved by fetching the document it names,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and on what terms. See ["},{"code":"CimdPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]; off unless somebody turns it on (I1). Nested, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"therefore inherited or overridden "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"whole"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the fields are terms of one decision, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"half-merged posture is one neither the organization nor the tenant wrote."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/cimd","title":"cimd","kind":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/init(cimd:dcrAllowedRedirectHosts:dcrAllowedScopes:dcrMaxClients:dcrUnusedClientTTLDays:defaultLocale:dynamicRegistration:externalClientAllowedResources:samlIdpEnabled:sensitiveScopesEnabled:ssfEnabled:ssfInactiveReason:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"cimd"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"CimdPolicy","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK10CimdPolicyV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"dcrAllowedRedirectHosts"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"]?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":